Earlier author-directed refinements explain how relevant capabilities of
existing methods enter a continuous generative model. The original DOCX is
unchanged. This release adds author-authorized clarifications in sections 2.3–2.4,
3.7, 7.2 and 7.5 and the matching introductory chain: reality versus its
records, cross-scale effects without new
levels, and the non-universal order of language-mediated cognition. Identities,
the baseline hash and refinements are recorded in references/source-map.json.
Version 7.1.0 also clarifies the opening state/reading example, task-relative
research stopping, intervention/action/plan versus scheduling, and the role of
conscious endorsement in human action. The original source DOCX is unchanged.

StateDyne AI Execution Specification v3.7 is preserved byte-for-byte under
engineering/ for explicit source review. It is an archive, not current runtime
instructions. Current execution responsibilities are independently reorganized
in SKILL.md and the task-activated reference modules. Version 7.0.0 replaces the
5.11 runtime, separates design from external execution authorization, supports
adaptive independent exploration, and replaces every-turn audit-form gates
with substantive review. The historical 6.0.0 experiment is not this release.
Version 7.1.0 strengthens visible intervention results, active information
acquisition and updating, conditional action design, quality-first operation,
capability activation by missing dependencies, and independent verification.
Version 7.2.0 retains the 7.1 method text unchanged. Runtime refinements add
explicit delivery of shared evidence without forcing a shared explanation,
dependency-driven independent and collaborative work, constructive interface
design, premise-aware updates, natural mainline continuity, and protection
against value loss through integration or review. Persistence remains dependent
on actual host operations; prompts do not provide a memory service or hard gate.
Version 7.3.0 preserves the complete 7.1/7.2 method and adds composite outcome
tracking, explicit delivery checks and an optional standard-library local state
tool for versioned declared dependencies, candidate records, artifacts and action
receipts. Its structural checks do not establish semantic truth, authorization,
external execution or real-world effectiveness, and do not control host sending.
UI-only semantic equivalence permits host YAML reserialization; release checking
continues to require exact bytes with --strict-bytes.

