Version 7.4.0 clarifies the author-requested synonymous use of intervention
point and leverage point in method section 6.1, retaining priority comparison.
Runtime changes cover concrete public wording, informative visuals, visible
intervention comparisons and actions, conversational continuation, source
boundaries and evidence-based persistent revision. No host-wide enforcement,
autonomous learning or general superiority is asserted.

Version 7.5.0 retains the 7.4.3 human-readable method byte-for-byte and
reorganizes execution responsibilities around task-grounded exploration,
information dependencies, action-supported intervention comparisons and
scope-aware conversational delivery. Cross-position action priorities are
compared before full planning; refusal to supply information preserves
conditional progress. No empirical superiority or guaranteed novelty is claimed.

Version 7.5.1 resolves delivery-scope ambiguity for broad change requests,
preserving same-turn action-supported intervention priorities while separating
their presentation from detailed actions and full plans. It strengthens natural
continuation, comparable alternatives, combination tradeoffs and the distinction
between a recommended action and its implementation steps. Prerequisites for
removing old arrangements and the scope of validation remain explicit. It checks
unprompted scope inference through multi-turn development tasks. The method and
state tools remain unchanged; no general performance guarantee is asserted.

Version 7.5.2 makes substantive open work quality-first by default and links
early information checking, independent exploration and exact-draft review to
actual host operations. It preserves observation scope, supports neutral recall
and late model-changing information, broadens meaningful intervention coverage
and compares genuinely interacting combinations before selection. Innovation
checks default assumptions and cross-path construction without manufacturing
novelty. Conditional plans and conversational continuation remain scope-aware.
The method and scripts are unchanged. Actual orchestration and content checks
are distinct; prompt instructions do not guarantee compliance or effectiveness.

Version 7.7.0 distinguishes conditional consequences from evidence-dependent
current judgments, tightens task-scoped information and assistance rules, and
requires useful generative consequences alongside evidential accuracy. Dialogue
and evaluation rules cover both premature advice and unnecessary deferral.
Method text, source archive and executable state scripts are unchanged.

Version 7.7.1 centers task-specific explanatory and generative gains, distinguishes
working explanations from established individual causes, extends conditional
consequences through adaptive responses, and reviews omitted substantive value
before minor expression. It consolidates existing responsibilities rather than
adding case-specific answers. The method and executable scripts are unchanged;
prompt compliance and general performance remain empirical questions.

Version 8.0.0 makes the evolving generative structure the shared runtime core.
Explanation, relational transformation, intervention discovery, concrete
prototypes and feedback revise the same inspectable results. Independent
generation and adversarial review have separate responsibilities. Evidence
requirements govern claims and adoption without extinguishing exploratory
construction. The complete method, archive and executable state tools are
unchanged. No universal innovation, empirical superiority or host-enforcement
guarantee is asserted.

Version 8.0.1 preserves evidence identity across direct observation, estimates,
counterfactuals and assistant-authored drafts. A central new relation must trace to
supporting and limiting material, survive a plain-language rewrite and produce a
consequence distinct from its strongest alternative. Uncertainty must open such
competing consequences instead of ending in a variable list. Review rejects
self-confirming evidence upgrades, decorative terms, formulas and tables, arbitrary
time windows and preventive advice without a change target or observed impairment.
The method, archive and executable support scripts are unchanged.

Version 8.0.2 carries the object, question position, time scope, material identity
and limits of a relation through synthesis, headlines, numeric ranges, summaries and
recommendations. Alternatives compete only when they answer the same explanatory
question at a compatible scope; connected formation, activation, persistence and
severity relations remain distinct. Composite contrasts cannot be decomposed into
individual causal effects during compression. It separates environmental trends,
path opportunities and subject-level net benefit, and distinguishes forecasts,
chosen decision deadlines and observation periods. User-supplied dates do not
justify themselves; unsupported calendars become event conditions rather than a
default choice of the later date. Review now works backward from the exact deliverable
to its weakest supporting premise and blocks preventive action created only by
imagined deterioration. The method, archive and executable support scripts are
unchanged.

Installed identity checking accepts only explicitly recorded, observed
host-materialized icon byte variants. Runtime, method and script identities
remain exact; strict release checking does not allow these variants.

Version 9.0.0 reconstructs runtime control around inspectable generative work,
real independent expansion, generation-quality review, targeted rework and
exact-deliverable review. Breadth, depth, relational innovation, information
updates and action-supported comparisons are primary outcome responsibilities.
The new check_work.py binds local file versions and review records; it does not
evaluate semantic quality, authenticate reviewers or control host sending.
Repeated caution rules are consolidated. The human-readable method, source
archive and existing state scripts remain byte-for-byte unchanged. No minimum
runtime, fixed iteration quota, forced novelty or universal advantage is claimed.

Version 9.1.0 refines mixed-request scope, analysis/intervention separation,
point-first delivery with feasible action support, open-ended valuable search,
plain continuation, optional recall and draft evidence identity. Reviews check
these outcomes as well as exact delivery. The method, archive, UI and executable
tools remain unchanged; no universal compliance or exhaustive-search claim is made.

Version 9.2.0 separates internal task and stage responsibility from user expression.
Points are evaluated through influenceability and value without a mandatory action
per point. Action design supports many-to-many effects and shared costs; plans
compare actual combinations. Continued generation may deepen, broaden, challenge,
recombine or construct, retaining useful alternatives beyond the current best.
Relevant cognitive, attention, meaning and learning routes enter alongside external
routes. Reviews check substantive generation, true stage completion and natural
delivery. Internal records do not prescribe user templates. The complete method,
archive, UI and executable support tools remain unchanged. No fixed search count,
guaranteed novelty, universal performance or host-enforcement claim is made.

Version 9.3.0 connects stage-specific deliverables through actual dependencies.
Prioritized intervention positions have internal feasible effect paths; coupled
positions compete with single positions before action and plan selection.
Positions, change directions, operations and plans remain distinct. Actions
explain their causal use, including meaning and adoption when people participate,
without making cognition a universal prerequisite. Single actions, combinations
and no added work compete. Review returns substantive failures to generation or
design before polishing language. Internal rigor and retained alternatives do
not become frontend templates; continuation identifies the actual next work.
The method, archive, UI and executable support tools remain unchanged. Small
development tests do not establish universal effectiveness or guaranteed novelty.

Version 9.4.0 selects public deliverables by requested scope while preserving
deeper internal comparison. Independently useful alternatives remain available
through value-based explanation, brief coverage and batching; expanded searches
deliver new value and affected revisions instead of repeating unchanged lists.
Optional neutral recall supports discovery beyond existing hypotheses without
suggesting experiences or blocking progress. Continuation distinguishes the next
work from further current-stage search. Review prioritizes semantic outcomes and
readable mechanisms over caution wording. The method, archive, UI and executable
support tools remain unchanged; limited tests do not guarantee general compliance.

Version 9.5.0 answers direct horizon questions at warranted temporal scales,
checks consequential prior personal conditions, and compares actions by the
requested outcome, effect horizon and added monitoring burden. Public answers
are reconstructed from useful relations rather than compressed internal records;
stage handoffs identify the next work without exporting its entire design.
Generation and delivery reviews share these outcome checks. The complete method,
source archive, UI and executable support tools remain unchanged. Development
observations do not establish treatment efficacy, universal quality or exhaustive
search.

Version 9.6.0 makes requested outcomes and substantive generative value the
operating priority, with truth, professional precision, safety and authorization
as continuous constraints. Consequential evidence relations stay separate from
public expression. Grounded leading explanations, competing futures and robust
cross-explanation results continue under uncertainty. Nine internal search
entrances cover dynamics through paradigms and local windows without replacing
the method's original nine categories. Goals and protected values govern
multi-layer leverage, action and plan comparisons across time scales. Open
industry and venture questions retain structural futures before validation or
implementation. Feedback has distinct evidential uses; dialogue tracks side
questions and resumes actual unfinished work. Reviews first test added value,
coverage and construction, then consequential grounding and expression. The
complete method, archived execution specification, UI and executable support
tools remain unchanged. Limited semantic checks establish neither universal
performance nor real-world intervention effectiveness. Private tests and
recovery materials are excluded from distribution.

Version 9.7.0 consolidates repeated defensive rules into positive outcome,
evidence and delivery responsibilities while preserving continuous truth,
professional, safety and authorization constraints. Breadth feeds explicit
relationship synthesis; preferred actions are supported by applicable evidence,
goal/time-matched effect paths and comparison with the strongest feasible
alternatives. Personal problems retain structural and paradigm construction
alongside mature approaches. Public qualifications are consequence-filtered,
known goals carry forward, and continuation follows actual unfinished work
rather than a mandatory dual invitation. Review repairs generation and ranking
before polishing language. Method text, source archive, UI and executable tools
are unchanged; no new modules, state fields or review rounds are added. Private
semantic outputs remain outside distribution. Limited forward checks do not
establish universal reliability, comparative superiority or treatment efficacy.

Version 9.8.0 connects action authority, competing feasible routes, adoption
formation and explanation carriers at existing runtime handoffs. Stage-specific
information, open futures and incremental continuation use existing records.
The method and archived specification remain byte-identical to 9.7.0. No private
case facts, prompts, answers or evaluation artifacts are distributed. Behavioral
observations are limited; this skill does not supply real-world state or execution.
Windows inventory and review reads preserve canonical paths and exact binary versions.

Version 9.8.1 narrows a user-facing language defect without changing the method
or generation architecture. Concision now comes from selecting and deduplicating
content rather than clipping complete words, compressing sentences into field-like
phrases, or assigning disposable new names to one-off relations. Dialogue, final
review and semantic evaluation apply the same boundary while preserving technical
terms, substantive relations, evidence and action value. Keyword scans are not
treated as proof of natural language quality. No private case material is included.

Version 9.8.2 closes three recurrent delivery failures already covered in principle
but not reliably caught in review. Numerical future ranges now require an actual
basis for both bounds, while useful event or magnitude judgments remain mandatory
when exact dating is unsupported. External claims are checked against the specific
source that carries each product fact, date, number, denominator and conclusion;
adjacent links cannot stand in for missing support. Final review removes unsolicited
monitoring, automation and service invitations unless they are the user's request
or a selected necessary action. The method, runtime architecture and public file
set remain unchanged, and no private case material is included.

Two parallel Version 9.8.3 distributions were derived from Version 9.8.2.
The earlier distribution moved consequential premise comparison to the first
ranking and to individual commitments, with review of the strongest feasible
alternative under credible competing conditions. The later distribution
consolidated human change and habit formation in method section 7.8, strengthened
substantive innovation and information acquisition, and reactivated action
comparison when an informed user requests further progress.

Version 9.8.4 integrates both distributions. Shared comparison duties run before
the first ranking or reranking and are revisited at later commitments and final
review. The later method and execution enhancements are retained. The public
file set, UI and executable support tools are unchanged. Private cases,
behavioral answers and development evidence are excluded. Limited observations
do not establish cross-model stability or real-world effectiveness.

Version 9.8.5 reorganizes per-turn restoration, independent generation duties,
all-candidate evidence updating, concentrated information acquisition and
target-based search when entering change. Immutable optional checkpoints add
portable checks for declared continuity; semantic quality remains a model
responsibility. Generation and exact-deliverable review may share one substantive
invocation. The method, archived specification, UI and established domain
mechanisms are retained. Private cases and evaluation artifacts are excluded.

Version 9.8.6 binds existing generative capabilities to task transitions: complete
first-wave results, synthesis-driven further search, counterfactual question
dependencies, formation and selection of generative relations, active omission
review and whole-plan dependency checks. The method and existing scripts remain
unchanged. Runtime instructions are not automatic host enforcement; real behavior
is evaluated separately. Private evidence is excluded from this distribution.

Version 9.8.8 derives solely from the 9.8.7 release. It prioritizes a compact
recoverable task state, detects responsibilities from actual answer content,
and targets missing outcomes before further orchestration or editorial work.
Goal-reopened action comparison, model reconstruction and bounded exploration
remain within the existing modules. The method, archive and helper code are
unchanged. Natural-language duties do not provide host enforcement, automatic
model routing or a guarantee of stable model or real-world performance.

